cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Trustworthy LLM Judges. Detecting Embedded Judgment Manipulation and Anchoring Verdicts with Confidential Computing"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the master thesis. A research prototype of an architecture in
  which a language model only proposes actions. A human approves the compiled plan, an
  independent reference monitor checks every step, an Authority issues single-use
  capabilities, and a gateway holds the credentials. Each step can run in its own attested
  Intel TDX virtual machine on Confidential Containers.
authors:
  - family-names: Felsch
    given-names: Jan-Frederik
license: MIT
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - prompt injection
  - reference monitor
  - capability tokens
  - confidential computing
  - remote attestation
